{0 The project template}

Copy [template/] outside the workero source checkout to start a Worker.
Follow {{!page-getting_started}Getting started} to install the source package
and run the copy locally.

{1 Files}

- [dune-project] requires OCaml 5.4 or later and the [workero] package.
- [src/dune] builds [src/main.ml] with [(modes wasm)] and links [workero].
- [src/main.ml] handles [GET /], [POST /echo], and [GET /env].
- [wrangler.toml] points to [_worker/index.js], runs
  [workero build src/main.bc.wasm.js], watches [src/], and sets [GREETING]
  in [[vars]].
- [package.json] lists Wrangler 4.151.3 and binaryen 132. binaryen supplies
  [wasm-opt] for wasm_of_ocaml.

{1 Run the copied project}

After installing the source package into your active opam switch, run these
commands from your copy:

{@sh[
eval "$(opam env)"
npm install
npx wrangler dev
]}

In another terminal, request [http://127.0.0.1:8787/]. Expect
[Hello from OCaml on Cloudflare Workers]. Request [/env] to see
[hello from vars], the default [GREETING] value.

To deploy, first run [npx wrangler login] with a Cloudflare account, then
[npx wrangler deploy]. You do not need an account for local [wrangler dev].
